/-! # Clearing denominators in a supplied local closed free model

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 01YB and 01YE, the ideal-lattice extension argument.
(blueprint: lem-pc-c3-coherent-local-free-ideal-lattice)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- A local map from a finite closed free source extends from an ideal lattice.
The lattice inclusion is invertible over the given open; no injectivity of the
extended map or generic stalk hypothesis on the target is asserted.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 01YB, applied to a closed free source as in the final
paragraph of Tag 01YE, and Tag 01Y6 for coherence of the closed free source.
(blueprint: lem-pc-c3-coherent-local-free-ideal-lattice)

Proof: set H = i_*(O_Z^{direct sum r}). On an affine Spec A with Z cut out by L,
its sections are (A/L)^r, hence finite over A. Closed pushforward preserves
quasi-coherence, so H is coherent. Let K be the reduced ideal of X minus U.
The coherent target F is quasi-coherent. Tag 01YB extends the supplied morphism
H|U -> F|U to a global map K^n H -> F agreeing with it on U. On Spec A the source
has sections (K(A)^n (A/L))^r. These identifications commute with localization,
so K^n H is i_*(I^{direct sum r}), where I is the nth power of the ideal on Z
generated by the image of K. This ideal is quasi-coherent on Noetherian Z,
therefore coherent. If n = 0 it is the unit ideal. Since K is the unit ideal on U,
I is the unit ideal on i inverse U. Thus the displayed lattice inclusion becomes
an isomorphism on U. Composing the source identification with the extended map
produces alpha, and the compatibility of that identification with inclusions gives
the displayed equality. This argument works for any phi, including zero, for
r = 0, and for U = X (where I may be the unit ideal and no denominators are needed).
The source Z need not be integral and U need not meet every component.
No choice of data from an unproved existence theorem occurs in a definition. -/
theorem coherent_local_free_ideal_lattice
    {X Z : Scheme.{u}} [IsNoetherian X]
    (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i]
    (F : X.Modules) (hF : RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace F)
    (r : ℕ) (U : X.Opens)
    (φ : (restrictFunctor U.ι).obj
        ((pushforward i).obj (∐ fun _ : Fin r => SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf)) ⟶
      (restrictFunctor U.ι).obj F) :
    ∃ (I : Z.IdealSheafData),
      RingedSpace.IsCoherent Z.toRingedSpace I.toModules ∧
      IsIso ((restrictFunctor U.ι).map
        ((pushforward i).map (Sigma.desc (fun j : Fin r ↦ I.toModulesι ≫
          Sigma.ι (fun _ : Fin r ↦ SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf) j)))) ∧
      ∃ (α : (pushforward i).obj (∐ fun _ : Fin r => I.toModules) ⟶ F),
        (restrictFunctor U.ι).map α =
          (restrictFunctor U.ι).map
            ((pushforward i).map (Sigma.desc (fun j : Fin r ↦ I.toModulesι ≫
          Sigma.ι (fun _ : Fin r ↦ SheafOfModules.unit Z.ringCatSheaf) j))) ≫ φ := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
